				\begin{document}$${{\Delta}}{F}_{{\rm{MTP}}}^{{\rm{liquid}}}(V,T)$$\end{document}ΔFMTPliquid(V,T), unfolds the liquid free energy surface in the volume and temperature dimensions. For that purpose, integration of the internal energy and pressure along the temperature and volume axis is performed (Fig. 1d and Eqs. (4), (5)). As for thermodynamic integration, also this calculation step has fewer requirements with respect to system size and time sampling than the interface method. The last term \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
